{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/EVENTS.md && rg --files lib && rg -n 'Analytics|analytics|Offer|offer|Registration|registration' lib\"","aggregated_output":"# Product events — registration funnel\n\nOwner: product. Status: approved, waiting for implementation.\n\nWe want to see where people drop out between opening the app and reading the\noffers. Each row is one event. Names are snake_case and must match exactly,\ndashboards and funnels are already built on them.\n\n| Event | When | Properties |\n|---|---|---|\n| `registration_email_started` | User started typing their email | — |\n| `registration_phone_started` | User started typing their phone number | — |\n| `loan_amount_changed` | User moved the loan amount slider | `amount` (int, the chosen amount) |\n| `terms_accepted` | User ticked the terms and conditions checkbox | — |\n| `registration_continue_tapped` | User tapped Continue on the registration screen | `amount` (int), `terms` (bool) |\n| `offers_scrolled` | User scrolled the offers list | `offset` (double, how far they scrolled) |\n\nNotes\n- Do not send the email or the phone number as properties (PII).\n- Screen views are already tracked automatically, no event needed for those.\n- The funnel is: email started → phone started → amount changed → terms\n  accepted → continue tapped → offers scrolled.\nlib/analytics.dart\nlib/main.dart\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart\nlib/analytics.dart:4:class Analytics {\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:3:class Offer {\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:4:  const Offer(this.bank, this.months, this.rate);\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:10:const _offers = [\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:11:  Offer('Norbank', 12, 9.9),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:12:  Offer('Norbank', 24, 10.4),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:13:  Offer('Fjordcredit', 12, 8.7),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:14:  Offer('Fjordcredit', 36, 11.2),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:15:  Offer('Vestkapital', 24, 9.5),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:16:  Offer('Vestkapital', 48, 12.0),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:17:  Offer('Sparbank', 12, 10.9),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:18:  Offer('Sparbank', 60, 12.8),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:19:  Offer('Nordlån', 36, 10.1),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:20:  Offer('Nordlån', 60, 12.3),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:23:class OfferScreen extends StatelessWidget {\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:24:  const OfferScreen({super.key});\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:29:      appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('Offers')),\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:31:        itemCount: _offers.length,\nlib/screens/offer_screen.dart:33:          final o = _offers[i];\nlib/main.dart:4:import 'analytics.dart';\nlib/main.dart:5:import 'screens/offer_screen.dart';\nlib/main.dart:6:import 'screens/registration_screen.dart';\nlib/main.dart:10:  await Analytics.init();\nlib/main.dart:25:          '/': (_) => const RegistrationScreen(),\nlib/main.dart:26:          '/offers': (_) => const OfferScreen(),\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:3:class RegistrationScreen extends StatefulWidget {\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:4:  const RegistrationScreen({super.key});\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:7:  State<RegistrationScreen> createState() => _RegistrationScreenState();\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:10:class _RegistrationScreenState extends State<RegistrationScreen> {\nlib/screens/registration_screen.dart:67:                  ? () => Navigator.of(context).pushNamed('/offers')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
